ct option is: B\n\nStep-by-Step Explanation:\n\n1. **Harry's Attributes**: Harry is big (6) and green (7).\n2. **Big and Green Things**: All big, green things are young (8). Since Harry is big and green, he is young.\n3. **Youngness and Coldness**: If Harry is young (13), he is cold.\n4. **Coldness and Furriness**: If Harry is cold and young, he is furry (14).\n5. **Furriness and Kindness**: All furry things are kind (12). Thus, Harry is kind.\n6. **Kindness and Redness**: If something is kind, it is not red (11). Therefore, Harry cannot be red.\n7. **Redness and Greenness**: All red things are green (10), but Harry is green, so he might not be red. However, since he's kind, he can't be red.\n\nConclusion: Harry is not red.\n\nThe correct option is: B",
