s: B) False\n\nStep-by-Step Explanation:\n\n1. Harry is smart (fact 7).\n2. Since Harry is smart, he is kind (fact 8).\n3. Being kind, Harry is quiet (fact 11).\n4. As Harry is quiet and smart, he must be blue (fact 9).\n5. However, if Harry is smart and blue, fact 14 states he must be red.\n6. This contradiction implies Harry cannot be blue.\n7. Therefore, the statement \"Harry is blue\" is false.\n\nAnswer: B) False",
