lso says that quiet people are kind. So, if Gary is quiet, he must be kind, which he is. But that doesn't necessarily mean he's quiet because we don't know if he's quiet or not. We just know he's kind and cold.\n\nSo, can we determine if Gary is quiet? Let's see. The only way Gary is quiet is if he's green, because all green people are quiet. But we don't know if Gary is green. The facts don't mention Gary's color. So, we can't conclude he's quiet based on the given information.\n\nTherefore, the statement \"Gary is quiet\" is unknown because we don't have enough information to confirm it.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C) Unknown",
