ent \"Erin is not round\" would be false. But wait, let me make sure I didn't miss anything.\n\nWait, point 12 says if someone is smart and not cold, they are rough. Erin is smart and cold, so she doesn't fall into that category. So she could be rough or not. But from point 10, since she's smart and furry, she must be round. So she is round.\n\nTherefore, the statement \"Erin is not round\" would be false because Erin is round.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False\n\nStep-by-Step Explanation:\n\n1. **Identify Erin's Attributes**: Erin is smart and cold.\n2. **Apply Rule 7**: Since Erin is smart and cold, she is white.\n3. **Apply Rule 5**: As Erin is white, she must be blue.\n4. **Apply Rule 11**: Being blue means Erin is smart, which aligns with her status.\n5. **Determine Furriness**: From Rule 8, all smart people are furry, so Erin is furry.\n6. **Apply Rule 10**: Since Erin is smart and furry, she is round.\n7. **Conclusion**: Erin is round, so the statement \"Erin is not round\" is false.\n\nAnswer: B) False",
