furry. Therefore, Harry is furry.\n\nBut the question is asking if Harry is not furry. So if Harry is definitely furry, then the statement \"Harry is not furry\" is false.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. Point 9 says all young people are furry. So Harry, being young, must be furry. Therefore, Harry is furry, so the statement \"Harry is not furry\" is false.\n\nBut wait, let me check if there's any other information that might affect this. For example, point 14 says furry people are rough. So if Harry is furry, he's rough. But does that affect anything else? Not directly, because we don't have information about Harry's other traits.\n\nSo, based on point 9, Harry is young, so he's furry. Therefore, the statement \"Harry is not furry\" is false.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False\n\nStep-by-Step Explanation:\n\n1. From the given facts, Harry is young (point 7).\n2. All young people are furry (point 9).\n3. Therefore, Harry is furry.\n4. The statement \"Harry is not furry\" is false.\n\nAnswer: B) False",
