he'd be cold (from \"quiet implies cold\").\n3. If Erin were big, she'd be cold (from \"all big things are cold\").\n4. If Erin is round, she can't be quiet (from \"all blue, round things are not quiet\").\n5. If Erin is round and quiet, she'd be cold, making her rough (from \"cold and rough implies furry\").\n6. However, we don't know if Erin is round, big, or quiet.\n7. Without knowing these, we can't confirm if she's furry.\n\nAnswer: C) Unknown",
