h we also knew.\n\nNow, from point 12, all rough, furry people are cold. Since Charlie is rough, if he's furry, he must be cold. But we don't know if he's cold yet.\n\nLooking at point 13, cold, nice people are big. Charlie is nice and big, so he must be cold. So Charlie is cold.\n\nNow, from point 12, since Charlie is rough and cold, and he's rough and furry, he must be cold. But we don't know if he's furry yet.\n\nWait, let's see if there's another way. From point 5, all big people are rough. Charlie is big, so he's rough. From point 8, if someone is nice and rough, they are kind. Charlie is nice and rough, so he's kind. From point 9, if Charlie is kind, he's big, which we already have.\n\nNow, from point 12, all rough, furry people are cold. So if Charlie is rough and furry, he's cold. But we don't know if he's furry yet.\n\nWait, maybe we can find another angle. From point 1, Anne is furry. From point 2, Bob is big and furry. From point 11, nice people are big. Charlie is nice, so he's big. From point 7, all kind, big people are rough. So if Charlie is kind, he's rough. But we already established he's rough because he's big.\n\nWait, maybe we can look at point 13 again. Cold, nice people are big. Charlie is nice and big, so he's cold. Now, from point 12, rough, furry people are cold. So if Charlie is rough and cold, he must be furry. Because if he were not furry, then being rough and cold wouldn't make him a rough, furry person, but we don't know if he's furry yet.\n\nWait, let me think again. From point 12, all rough, furry people are cold. So if Charlie is rough and cold, then he must be furry. Because if he were not furry, he wouldn't be a rough, furry person, so the statement doesn't apply. But since he's rough and cold, he must be furry.\n\nSo, putting it all together:\n\n- Charlie is nice (given).\n- Nice people are big (point 11), so Charlie is big.\n- All big people are rough (point 6), so Charlie is rough.\n- If Charlie is nice and rough, he's kind (point 8), so he's kind.\n- If Charlie is kind, he's big (point 9), which we already have.\n- Now, since Charlie is rough and kind, he's cold (point 10).\n- Charlie is nice, big, rough, and cold.\n- From point 13, cold, nice people are big, which we have.\n- From point 12, rough, furry people are cold. Since Charlie is rough and cold, he must be furry.\n\nTherefore, Charlie is furry.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A) True\n\nStep-by-Step Explanation:\n\n1. **Charlie is nice** (given).\n2. **Nice people are big** (point 11), so Charlie is big.\n3. **All big people are rough** (point 6), so Charlie is rough.\n4. **If Charlie is nice and rough**, he is kind (point 8). Since he's nice and rough, he's kind.\n5. **If Charlie is kind**, he is big (point 9), which aligns with point 2.\n6. **Charlie is cold** because he's nice and rough (point 10).\n7. **From point 12**, rough, furry people are cold. Since Charlie is rough and cold, he must be furry.\n\nAnswer: A) True",
