on't have any information that contradicts this. So, putting it all together, since Anne is furry and furry things are nice, she must be nice. Therefore, the statement \"Anne is nice\" is true.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nStep-by-Step Explanation:\n\n1. **Anne is Furry (Point 2):** From the given information, Anne is described as furry.\n\n2. **Furry Things are Nice (Point 10):** This rule states that if a thing is furry, it is also nice.\n\n3. **Conclusion:** Since Anne is furry, according to the rule, she must be nice.\n\nTherefore, the statement \"Anne is nice\" is true.\n\nThe correct option is: A",
