d smart, then they are furry. So, if Harry is green and smart, he must be furry. But we don't know if Harry is green.\n\nLooking at fact 10 again: If someone is smart, they are kind. Harry is smart, so he's kind, which is consistent.\n\nBut the question is about Harry being green. The facts don't provide any direct information about Harry's color. We know Harry is kind and smart, but nothing about his color. There's no statement that links Harry's color to anything else, except that if he were green, he'd be furry (from fact 13). But we don't know if he's green or not.\n\nSo, based on the given information, we can't determine if Harry is green or not. There's no direct evidence or logical deduction that leads us to conclude whether Harry is green or not. Therefore, the statement is unknown.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C) Unknown",
