5), he must be furry. So, Bob is smart and furry.\n\nFrom fact 13, being furry implies being young. So, Bob is young. Now, from fact 16, if Bob is young, then he is nice. Therefore, Bob is nice.\n\nSo, the statement \"Bob is not nice\" would be false because Bob is nice.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B\n\nStep-by-Step Explanation:\n\n1. **Determine Bob's Attributes:**\n   - Bob is blue (Fact 1).\n   - Bob is round (Fact 2).\n   - Bob is smart (Fact 15, since all round things are smart).\n\n2. **Determine Bob's Age:**\n   - From Fact 13, being furry implies being young. Since Bob is smart (Fact 15) and all smart things are furry (Fact 11), Bob is furry.\n   - Therefore, Bob is young (from Fact 13).\n\n3. **Determine Bob's Niceness:**\n   - From Fact 16, if Bob is young, then he is nice.\n   - Since Bob is young, he is nice.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - The statement \"Bob is not nice\" is false because Bob is indeed nice.\n\nAnswer: B) False",
