point 15), so this rule doesn't apply.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the squirrel is red and round, so it chases the dog. The dog, by point 22, chases the bald eagle. The bald eagle chases the squirrel. So, the squirrel is chasing the dog, which is chasing the bald eagle, and the bald eagle is chasing the squirrel. This creates a cycle where both the squirrel and the bald eagle are chasing each other.\n\nTherefore, the statement \"The squirrel chases the bald eagle\" is true.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nStep-by-Step Explanation:\n\n1. From point 2, the bald eagle chases the squirrel.\n2. Point 23 states that if the bald eagle sees the squirrel and chases it, the squirrel is red. Since the squirrel is red (point 15), this condition is met.\n3. Point 17 indicates that a red and round object (the squirrel) chases the dog.\n4. Point 22 states that if the squirrel chases the dog, it also chases the bald eagle.\n5. Therefore, the squirrel chases the bald eagle.\n\nAnswer: A) True",
